// An install over a HOF parameter whose effect instance arrives through
// the parameter: `g(f) = (f()) ~> runit`, and the caller's closure performs
// `emit(5)` where runit's arm calls its payload as a function. The contract
// is the refusal — an Int is not a function.
//
// Measured 2026-09-23 through the pinned boot: check clean, then a runtime
// trap ("uninitialized element": 5 called). The direct form (the closure's
// body written inside `g`) refuses with E_TypeMismatch. The install unified
// its handled instance with the body's instances once, when the parameter's row
// was still empty; the instance that arrives at the call site never meets the
// arm's. Retires when a mask carries the handled instance and every arrival
// across it unifies (Hβ.effects.rows-are-propagated-cells).
effect Emit { emit(x: a) -> Int }
handler runit { emit(x) => resume(x()) }
fn g(f) = (f()) ~> runit
fn main() = g(() => emit(5))
